diff --git a/docs/grub-dev.texi b/docs/grub-dev.texi
index d7e2ec919..2fc4121c0 100644
--- a/docs/grub-dev.texi
+++ b/docs/grub-dev.texi
@@ -2487,6 +2487,59 @@ Optionally at the end of the file @samp{fini}, if it exists, is called with just
 the context. If you return no error during any of @samp{init}, @samp{write} and
 @samp{fini} then the file is considered as having succeded verification.
 
+@heading In-place Verification and Measurement
+
+By default, the verifier framework copies every opened file into a private heap
+buffer, runs the verifiers on that copy, and then serves all subsequent reads
+from it. This ensures that unverified data never reaches its final destination,
+preventing Time-of-Check to Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) vulnerabilities. However, for
+large files like an @samp{initrd} (often tens or hundreds of megabytes), this
+doubled the peak memory usage, since both the verifier framework and the bootloader
+kept separate copies of the file in memory.
+
+For verifiers that do not gate or authenticate the boot process (such as
+measurement-style verifiers like TPM and TPCM), it is safe to run verification
+directly on the loaded buffer inside the caller's memory, avoiding the need for
+a private copy.
+
+To support this optimization, the verifier structure @code{struct grub_file_verifier}
+has a boolean member @code{in_place}:
+
+@itemize
+@item @code{in_place}
+Should be set to @code{true} if the verifier only measures or hashes the file (like TPM
+or TPCM) rather than deciding whether the file is allowed to be loaded or run. Gating or
+authenticating verifiers (e.g., PGP, @samp{shim_lock}, or @samp{appendedsig}) @strong{must}
+leave this field set to @code{false}.
+@end itemize
+
+When a bootloader or loader wants to verify a file in place, it must use the following
+procedure:
+
+@enumerate
+@item Open the file with @code{grub_file_open()} using the type flag
+@code{GRUB_FILE_TYPE_VERIFY_IN_PLACE}. This flag @strong{must} be combined with
+@code{GRUB_FILE_TYPE_NO_DECOMPRESS}.
+
+@item If all registered and active verifiers are marked as @code{in_place}, the verifiers
+framework defers verification during the open stage and sets the tracking field
+@code{verify_pending} on the @code{grub_file_t} structure.
+
+@item If even one active verifier does not support @code{in_place}, the framework
+automatically falls back to normal open-time verification and reads the entire file
+into a private buffer.
+
+@item The loader must allocate the destination buffer, read or load the file into it,
+and then execute the deferred verification by calling:
+@code{grub_verify_in_place (file, buf, size)}
+before the file is closed. This function executes all deferred in-place verifiers
+on the loaded buffer and clears the @code{verify_pending} field.
+
+@item If the file is closed via @code{grub_file_close()} while @code{verify_pending}
+is still set to @code{1}, a warning is logged to the @samp{verify} debug stream, indicating
+that the loader forgot to call @code{grub_verify_in_place()}.
+@end enumerate
+
 @node Lockdown framework
 @chapter Lockdown framework
 
